  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A scrap shelf accepts clean usable offcuts, and examples show what fits each labeled container.\", \"decision\": \"How should usable offcuts enter the shared scrap supply?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nMembers place usable offcuts directly into the labeled scrap containers after comparing them with the examples. Materials become available immediately, with the person who created them doing the initial sorting work.\nMembers leave usable offcuts in a review tray, and the steward sorts them into labeled scrap containers each day. A consistent review keeps unsuitable pieces from becoming mixed into the shared supply.\nMembers offer usable offcuts at a brief end-of-session exchange before placing unclaimed pieces in labeled scrap containers. Someone with an immediate use can take material before it joins the longer-term scrap supply."
    }
  ],
